<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarifa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarifa is a town at the southern tip of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a> in the province of Cádiz, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-gibraltar">Strait of Gibraltar</a>. Named after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> commander Tarif ibn Malik, who landed there in 710, it was captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-iv-of-castile">Sancho IV of Castile</a> in 1292 and famously defended by Alonso Pérez de Guzmán in 1294. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rio-salado">Battle of Río Salado</a> nearby in 1340 ended major Marinid intervention in Spain.</p></div>
